      "USB-C in and out plus USB-A, IP67 rated"
    ],
    "cons": [
      "About 28 hours of sun to refill, five or six clear days",
      "About 5 hours at full brightness",
      "USB-C charge takes 5 to 6 hours"
    ],
    "bottomLine": "Buy it for a multi-day reserve and a real phone top-up, not for a fast solar refill.",
    "description": "The Luci Charge 360 is the big inflatable in BioLite's range. Its 4,000 mAh (14.8 Wh) battery is double the Charge 150, and its 31 warm white LEDs are rated at up to 360 lumens, bright enough to light a kitchen table. BioLite lists about 110 hours on low and about 5 hours on high. The catch is the refill: the panel is rated at about 28 hours of direct sun to full, and USB-C at 5 to 6 hours, because the battery is bigger but the panel collects energy at about the same rate as the smaller Lucis. That makes the 360 a reserve tank. Charge it full before storm season, run it on low or medium, and it can carry a household through several dark evenings while still having enough left to add most of a phone charge through its USB-C or USB-A output. It weighs 10.1 ounces and is IP67 rated."
  },
  {
