        <!-- Closing -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Buy a solar lantern for the days after the outlets are gone, and pick it by its solar recharge time as much as its lumens. The LuminAID Max 2-in-1 is the best all-round choice for outages, with a phone-charging battery and a panel that keeps up with moderate use. The BioLite Luci Charge 150 is the best USB-C alternative, the Luci Charge 360 is the one for a long, bright reserve, and the Luci Original is the cheap, light nightly lantern to buy in multiples.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Whatever you choose, charge it from USB before you store it, run it on low or medium, and keep a real power bank for the phones. A solar lantern does one job very well: it keeps giving you light long after everything else has gone flat.
          </p>
